# Gate step 1087-h2z9 — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# WHY THIS ONE IS IN --check AND NOT ONLY IN --ci-full, which would be the
# obvious place for a check about --ci-full: a difference between the two gates
# that is only detectable by the slower gate is detectable once a day, which is
# the exact accumulation window this packet is about. It has to run where every
# host runs.
#
# It is a set comparison over two files plus a small data file — sub-second, no
# build artifact, no podman, no network. See the fixture header for why the
# untriaged count ratchets rather than redding: there were 22 on the day it was
# written, and a gate that reds trunk on day one gets switched off.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose: a binding assembled from a
# variable is invisible to every name-based scan, including the
# bound-or-retired guard (1063-nraf). Keep it a plain string.
STEP_DESC="Checking every landing-gate/release-gate difference is declared (1087-h2z9)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-gate-divergence-is-declared.sh"
STEP_ERROR="a check runs in --ci-full and not in --check without being declared, or the untriaged ratchet turned the wrong way (1087-h2z9) — see the verdict line above"
STEP_OK="Gate-divergence declaration check passed"
